.TH "PERFORMANCECONTAINERTIMING.SIZE" "3JS" "October 26, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
PerformanceContainerTiming.size \- PerformanceContainerTiming: size
property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]size\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]PerformanceContainerTiming\f[R] interface returns the total area
of the container\(cqs accumulated painted region, calculated since the
container root was registered.
.SH VALUE
An integer representing a cumulative area in square CSS pixels.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[CR]size\f[R] reflects only the actual painted area within the
container, and omits content that was outside the viewport when it was
painted.
This differs from \f[CR]intersectionRect\f[R], which is a single
bounding rectangle and so can include gaps where no painting has
occurred.
Paired with \f[CR]intersectionRect\f[R], \f[CR]size\f[R] provides a
useful \f[I]indication\f[R] of how much of a container has rendered and
become visible so far.
It can also be used during debugging to confirm whether a container\(cqs
content is painting inside the viewport.
.PP
For more information, see When are entries generated?
in \f[CR]PerformanceContainerTiming\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
See Observing that only visible paints are counted in
\f[CR]PerformanceContainerTiming.intersectionRect\f[R].
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]PerformanceContainerTiming.intersectionRect\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
